Package: ClassifyR
Type: Package
Title: Binary Classification Ensemble with Five Machine Learning Algorithms
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    c(
      person("Yibing", "Zhang", email = "123090837@link.cuhk.edu.cn", role = c("aut", "cre")),
      person("Xinyi", "Hu", email = "123090188@link.cuhk.edu.cn", role = "aut"),
      person("Zijin", "Li", email = "123090312@link.cuhk.edu.cn", role = "aut")
    )
Maintainer: Yibing Zhang <123090837@link.cuhk.edu.cn>
Description: A comprehensive R package for binary classification tasks using five 
    machine learning algorithms: Support Vector Machines (SVM), 
    Decision Trees, Random Forest, XGBoost, and Neural Networks.
    The package provides an end-to-end pipeline including data preprocessing, model training, performance evaluation, and model comparison. 
    Features include standardized evaluation metrics (accuracy, precision, recall, F1, AUC-ROC), visualization tools 
    for model comparison, and interpretability methods (feature importance, decision rules).
